1.1.m:
And therefore listen to this summary: Nārāyaṇa is this entire Purāṇa;
even at the time of conjunction he makes the path, and at the time of dissolution it does not exist again.

Thus ends the first chapter named 'Summary of Contents' in the first quarter, the Prakriyāpāda, in the first part proclaimed by Vāyu in the glorious Brahmāṇḍa Mahāpurāṇa.

1.6.m:
Then that Brahmā becomes the thousand-eyed, thousand-footed,
thousand-headed Puruṣa, golden-hued, with subdued senses;
and in this regard they cite this verse concerning Nārāyaṇa:

The great sages beginning with Bhṛgu, as indicated at that time,
and eight great sages beginning with Satya, when the kalpa was dissolved;
then, while being transformed by them, the great [ocean] was completely surrounded by the supreme.
